{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Treat node1:/etc/inventory/app.conf as authoritative and synchronize its contents to node2 within 15 minutes of a change.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The initially absent source was established on node1, and node2 was configured for one-way pulls. A post-restart source change at 12:23:06 appeared automatically on node2 by 12:24:11, with matching SHA-256 hashes—about 65 seconds later. Cron execution and recovered scheduler state were also directly observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4b6bf80e1f784373","cmd-a0f01f37e1d246bc","cmd-dc3fcd4caba54c3a","cmd-85f170242eae485d","cmd-a4992d3b7d854cd0"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. The synchronization mechanism used and successfully executed the platform's existing shell, cron, SCP, and OpenSSH facilities before and after restarts.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-a7b8f1f8d6c74b0e","cmd-845c8aaddc1b44e4"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"Task-related configuration was focused, both nodes ended with no failed services, and no new listening sockets were introduced. The restart protocol was complete: each node had a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, a changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered services, data, and synchronization. Hygiene deductions: validation text appended to the authoritative configuration and later revised remained in the final file rather than being cleaned up (cmd-218cccedcd214fd5, cmd-85f170242eae485d); unnecessary /tmp/inventory-reboot.log files created by both restart commands also remained (cmd-9d85ab74562a42c2, cmd-6d44db4b13944063). Additionally, the retained synchronization key was authorized without forced-command or source restrictions, granting broader node1 access than file reading required (cmd-a72ed55656234f1a). The initial defective script deployment was promptly superseded by the corrected implementation and left no demonstrated conflicting service.","evidence_ids":["cmd-218cccedcd214fd5","cmd-85f170242eae485d","cmd-9d85ab74562a42c2","cmd-6d44db4b13944063","cmd-a72ed55656234f1a","cmd-387d12bea87f4105","cmd-a0f01f37e1d246bc","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct post-restart testing demonstrated one-way propagation from node1 to node2 in about 65 seconds, and both systems retained their original RHEL 7.9 release and kernel. Provider-wide restart evidence is complete and agrees with the fixed lifecycle boot identities. Minor hygiene concerns remain around test/log residue and an overly broad SSH authorization.","limitations":["Native package-health observations timed out both before and after execution, so package-manager consistency could not be independently assessed.","The authoritative file was absent initially and was created with placeholder comments; the evidence therefore proves synchronization of the newly established source, not preservation of pre-existing application configuration.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the task-specific script, cron file, or SSH authorization; their final state is supported by the executor's direct post-restart commands."]}
